From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Taozuhong <taozuhong@hotmail.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 08:30:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] MinGW: guard GtkPrinter usages in WebKitPrintOperation.cpp
 when GTK_UNIX_PRINTING is unset

Update 33 (fixing the round-33 CLANG64/CLANGARM64 WebKitPrintOperation.cpp
13-error block at [8285/8564]):

WebKitPrintOperation.cpp uses GtkPrinter, gtk_enumerate_printers(),
gtk_print_job_new(), gtk_print_job_set_source_fd(), gtk_print_job_send()
and friends from <gtk/gtkunixprint.h>, which the file includes only
under `#if HAVE(GTK_UNIX_PRINTING)`. The Round-23 OS(WINDOWS) stub for
webkitPrintOperationSendPagesToPrintPortal() (the freedesktop.org
portal path) bypassed the portal-specific surface, but several other
code paths in the same TU still name GtkPrinter unconditionally:

  * struct _WebKitPrintOperationPrivate::printer (line ~97): a member
    typed GRefPtr<GtkPrinter>;
  * webkitPrintOperationFinished(): `priv->printJob = nullptr;
    priv->data = { };` (the two members themselves are guarded above
    in the struct, but these two assignments were not);
  * webkitPrintOperationPrintPagesForFrame(): the function signature
    takes GtkPrinter* (the body was already guarded by
    `#if HAVE(GTK_UNIX_PRINTING)` at line 376, but the signature was
    not);
  * findFilePrinter() / printerFromSettingsOrDefault(): two static
    helpers returning GRefPtr<GtkPrinter> and calling
    gtk_enumerate_printers() unconditionally;
  * webkit_print_operation_print(): local `GRefPtr<GtkPrinter> printer
    = printerFromSettingsOrDefault(...)` plus a call into
    webkitPrintOperationPrintPagesForFrame(printer.get(), ...).

The MSYS2 GTK4 build does not ship gtk4-unix-print (the Unix print
backend is Linux-specific), so HAVE(GTK_UNIX_PRINTING) is unset on
all three MSYS2 MinGW environments, and the include of
<gtk/gtkunixprint.h> is skipped. The 13 undeclared-identifier errors
on the CLANG64/CLANGARM64 runners (lines 97, 342, 343, 369, 422, 425,
428, 847, 851, 854, 898) all reproduce against this shape.

The fix adds a forward declaration `typedef struct _GtkPrinter
GtkPrinter;` under `#else` of the existing `#if HAVE(GTK_UNIX_PRINTING)`
include block, so the type is at least known (as an opaque GObject-
derived pointer) when the GTK4 Unix print backend is absent. GRefPtr's
default traits call g_object_ref_sink()/g_object_unref() (which take
gpointer), so GRefPtr<GtkPrinter> compiles with just the forward
declaration; the refcount semantics are correct because GtkPrinter is
a GObject subtype on platforms where it is fully defined, and the
type is never instantiated on platforms where it is not.

The function bodies that actually call into gtk_enumerate_printers()
or gtk_print_job_*() are then guarded:

  * webkitPrintOperationFinished(): the two member-assignment lines
    are wrapped in `#if HAVE(GTK_UNIX_PRINTING)` (the members
    themselves are already guarded in the struct).
  * findFilePrinter(): the full function moves under
    `#if HAVE(GTK_UNIX_PRINTING)`, with a MinGW stub returning
    nullptr in `#else`.
  * printerFromSettingsOrDefault(): same shape as findFilePrinter().

The webkitPrintOperationPrintPagesForFrame() signature was already
fine (the body's GTK_UNIX_PRINTING guard makes the function a no-op
that falls into the `if (!printer)` early-return branch when the type
is opaque). The webkit_print_operation_print() call sites compile
because the stub helpers return nullptr, which the existing
`if (!printer)` guard turns into a clean error signal.

Sandbox verification: pre-patch source reproduces all 13 errors
against a synthesized MSYS2 CLANG64 configuration (HAVE(GTK_UNIX_PRINTING)
unset, <gtk/gtkunixprint.h> not on the include path); post-patch
source compiles cleanly with the same configuration (the forward
declaration is the only new symbol, and the function bodies are
removed by the preprocessor).

---
 Source/WebKit/UIProcess/API/gtk/WebKitPrintOperation.cpp | 31 ++++++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 30 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/Source/WebKit/UIProcess/API/gtk/WebKitPrintOperation.cpp b/Source/WebKit/UIProcess/API/gtk/WebKitPrintOperation.cpp
index 732ebf9..c5ec6c5 100644
--- a/Source/WebKit/UIProcess/API/gtk/WebKitPrintOperation.cpp
+++ b/Source/WebKit/UIProcess/API/gtk/WebKitPrintOperation.cpp
@@ -47,6 +47,16 @@
 
 #if HAVE(GTK_UNIX_PRINTING)
 #include <gtk/gtkunixprint.h>
+#else
+/* MinGW: GTK4 Unix print backend (gtk/gtkunixprint.h) is not shipped by the
+ * MSYS2 GTK4 build, so HAVE(GTK_UNIX_PRINTING) is unset and GtkPrinter is
+ * not declared. Several function signatures and local variables in this
+ * file still name GtkPrinter (the dialog-less print path, the file-printer
+ * lookup, the print-pages-for-frame helper); an opaque forward declaration
+ * lets them compile, while the function bodies that actually call into
+ * gtk_enumerate_printers()/gtk_print_job_*() are guarded below and
+ * replaced with stubs that report printing as unsupported. */
+typedef struct _GtkPrinter GtkPrinter;
 #endif
 
 using namespace WebKit;
@@ -339,8 +349,10 @@ static void webkitPrintOperationFinished(WebKitPrintOperation* printOperation)
 static void webkitPrintOperationFinished(WebKitPrintOperation* printOperation)
 {
     auto* priv = printOperation->priv;
+#if HAVE(GTK_UNIX_PRINTING)
     priv->printJob = nullptr;
     priv->data = { };
+#endif
 
     g_signal_emit(printOperation, signals[FINISHED], 0);
 }
@@ -419,6 +431,7 @@ static void webkitPrintOperationPrintPagesForFrame(WebKitPrintOperation* printOp
 #endif
 }
 
+#if HAVE(GTK_UNIX_PRINTING)
 static GRefPtr<GtkPrinter> findFilePrinter(GtkPrintSettings* settings)
 {
     struct FindPrinterData {
@@ -439,6 +452,15 @@ static GRefPtr<GtkPrinter> findFilePrinter(GtkPrintSettings* settings)
 
     return data.printer;
 }
+#else
+static GRefPtr<GtkPrinter> findFilePrinter(GtkPrintSettings*)
+{
+    /* MinGW stub: without GTK_UNIX_PRINTING there is no gtk_enumerate_printers
+     * and no GtkPrintBackendFile to discover; the portal path that calls this
+     * helper is also stubbed above for OS(WINDOWS). */
+    return nullptr;
+}
+#endif
 
 struct PrintPortalJobData {
     GRefPtr<WebKitPrintOperation> printOperation;
@@ -844,6 +866,7 @@ WebKitPrintOperationResponse webkit_print_operation_run_dialog(WebKitPrintOperat
     return webkitPrintOperationRunDialogForFrame(printOperation, parent, page.mainFrame());
 }
 
+#if HAVE(GTK_UNIX_PRINTING)
 static GRefPtr<GtkPrinter> printerFromSettingsOrDefault(GtkPrintSettings* settings)
 {
     struct FindPrinterData {
@@ -867,6 +890,13 @@ static GRefPtr<GtkPrinter> printerFromSettingsOrDefault(GtkPrintSettings* settin
 
     return data.printer;
 }
+#else
+static GRefPtr<GtkPrinter> printerFromSettingsOrDefault(GtkPrintSettings*)
+{
+    /* MinGW stub: see findFilePrinter() above. */
+    return nullptr;
+}
+#endif
 
 /**
  * webkit_print_operation_print:
-- 
2.39.1

From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Taozuhong <taozuhong@hotmail.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 09:25:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] MinGW: drop pre-Round-27 HANDLE-style Identifier construction
 in ProcessLauncherGLib.cpp

Update 34 (fixing the round-34 CLANG64/CLANGARM64 ProcessLauncherGLib.cpp
1-error block at [8347]/[8293]):

ProcessLauncherGLib.cpp:330 fails with
  error: no matching constructor for initialization of 'IPC::Connection::Identifier'
  didFinishLaunchingProcess(m_processID, IPC::Connection::Identifier {
    reinterpret_cast<HANDLE>(static_cast<intptr_t>(serverSocketValue)) });
                                                 ^  ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
The clang++ candidate list (Connection.h:298/300/301/305/309) shows only
the USE(UNIX_DOMAIN_SOCKETS) branch's constructors:
  * Identifier() = default
  * Identifier(Identifier&&) = default
  * explicit Identifier(Handle&&)              -> takes ConnectionHandle
  * explicit Identifier(UnixFileDescriptor&&)  -> takes UnixFileDescriptor
The OS(WINDOWS)-branch constructor `explicit Identifier(HANDLE handle)`
at Connection.h:320 is NOT in the candidate set, which means the
preprocessor picked the USE(UNIX_DOMAIN_SOCKETS) branch.

Root cause: Round 27 (commit b9c8176, "unify MinGW GTK IPC to unix-flavored
attachment/semaphore types") changed PlatformUse.h to unconditionally
#define USE_UNIX_DOMAIN_SOCKETS=1 for PLATFORM(GTK)||PLATFORM(WPE) on
Windows, so the MinGW GTK build picks the unix-flavored Identifier
(UnixFileDescriptor payload wrapping a Win32 SOCKET handle) and the
OS(WINDOWS)-branch Identifier(HANDLE) constructor disappears. The
existing ConnectionGLib.cpp was rewritten to the unix flavor in
Round 27 (six call sites in Update 27), and AuxiliaryProcessMain.cpp:110
was migrated in Round 28. The `#if OS(WINDOWS)` block at
ProcessLauncherGLib.cpp:328-336 was a pre-Round-27 leftover that the
flavor migration missed — it still constructs Identifier from a raw
HANDLE, which the unified Identifier class no longer has a constructor
for.

Fix: drop the `#if OS(WINDOWS) ... #else ... #endif` block at
ProcessLauncherGLib.cpp:328-336 and use the unix-flavored code path
on Windows too. The kept code is byte-identical to the original
pre-0003 code (which was the `#else` branch):

    RunLoop::mainSingleton().dispatch([protectedThis = protect(*this),
        this, serverSocket = WTF::move(webkitSocketPair.server)] mutable {
        didFinishLaunchingProcess(m_processID,
            IPC::Connection::Identifier { WTF::move(serverSocket) });
    });

webkitSocketPair.server is a UnixFileDescriptor (IPCUtilities.h:55-58
defines `struct SocketPair { UnixFileDescriptor client; UnixFileDescriptor
server; }` under `#if USE(UNIX_DOMAIN_SOCKETS) || OS(WINDOWS)`), and
Identifier(UnixFileDescriptor&&) is the constructor the kept code
invokes. The Win32 SOCKET handle packed inside the UnixFileDescriptor
is created by `IPC::createPlatformConnection()` (also in
IPCUtilities.h) which on Windows returns a bound UDP loopback socket
pair (the Round 22 / Round 27 winsock datagram IPC path).

The `#include <windows.h>` added by 0003 at the top of the file is
still needed: terminateProcess() further down uses OpenProcess() /
TerminateProcess() / CloseHandle() / HANDLE / DWORD / PROCESS_TERMINATE
under its own `#if OS(WINDOWS)` guard, and that block is correct as-is
(pure Win32 process control, not IPC flavor-dependent).

Sandbox verification: pre-patch source reproduces the
`no matching constructor for initialization of 'IPC::Connection::Identifier'`
error against a synthesized MSYS2 CLANG64 configuration
(USE(UNIX_DOMAIN_SOCKETS)=1 + OS(WINDOWS)=1, matching PlatformUse.h
on MinGW GTK). Post-patch source compiles cleanly: the kept code
constructs Identifier(UnixFileDescriptor&&), which is in the active
USE(UNIX_DOMAIN_SOCKETS) branch. `patch -Np1 --dry-run` on
pristine+0001-0007 applies with 0 .rej / 0 fuzz.

---
 .../Launcher/glib/ProcessLauncherGLib.cpp         | 8 +-------
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 7 deletions(-)

diff --git a/Source/WebKit/UIProcess/Launcher/glib/ProcessLauncherGLib.cpp b/Source/WebKit/UIProcess/Launcher/glib/ProcessLauncherGLib.cpp
index cda05b2..a3b5f1c 100644
--- a/Source/WebKit/UIProcess/Launcher/glib/ProcessLauncherGLib.cpp
+++ b/Source/WebKit/UIProcess/Launcher/glib/ProcessLauncherGLib.cpp
@@ -325,15 +325,9 @@ void ProcessLauncher::launchProcess()
     m_processID = g_ascii_strtoll(processIdStr, nullptr, 0);
     RELEASE_ASSERT(m_processID);
 
-#if OS(WINDOWS)
-    RunLoop::mainSingleton().dispatch([protectedThis = protect(*this), this, serverSocketValue = webkitSocketPair.server.release()] mutable {
-        didFinishLaunchingProcess(m_processID, IPC::Connection::Identifier { reinterpret_cast<HANDLE>(static_cast<intptr_t>(serverSocketValue)) });
-    });
-#else
     RunLoop::mainSingleton().dispatch([protectedThis = protect(*this), this, serverSocket = WTF::move(webkitSocketPair.server)] mutable {
         didFinishLaunchingProcess(m_processID, IPC::Connection::Identifier { WTF::move(serverSocket) });
     });
-#endif
 }
 
 void ProcessLauncher::terminateProcess()
-- 
2.39.1

From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Taozuhong <taozuhong@hotmail.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 10:45:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] MinGW: declare GLFence unix-only methods portably + add Windows stubs

Update 35a (fixing the round-35 CLANG64 AcceleratedSurface.cpp 3-error
block at [8333/8564]):

AcceleratedSurface.cpp:233/248/257 fails with
  error: no member named 'importFD' in 'WebCore::GLFence'
  error: no member named 'createExportable' in 'WebCore::GLFence'
  error: no member named 'exportFD' in 'WebCore::GLFence'

GLFence.h declares these three methods only under #if OS(UNIX):
  * static std::unique_ptr<GLFence> createExportable(const GLDisplay&);
  * static std::unique_ptr<GLFence> importFD(const GLDisplay&, WTF::UnixFileDescriptor&&);
  * virtual WTF::UnixFileDescriptor exportFD() { return { }; }

On MinGW GTK (OS(WINDOWS)=1), the OS(UNIX) guard skips all three
declarations, so any consumer that names them (AcceleratedSurface.cpp
at lines 233/248/257, plus CoordinatedPlatformLayerBufferDMABuf.cpp
and OpenXRGraphicsBindingOpenGLES.cpp on the Linux DMABuf / OpenXR
paths) fails to compile.

Fix: drop the OS(UNIX) guards in GLFence.h. UnixFileDescriptor is
portable to MinGW since Round 22 (Win32 SOCKET packed in the
descriptor payload), so the include and the signatures are safe on
every port. In GLFence.cpp, keep the Unix implementation paths
under OS(UNIX) (they call GLFenceEGL::createExportable /
GLFenceEGL::importFD which depend on ANDROID_native_fence_sync, a
Linux DMA-Buf/EGL extension that MSYS2 GTK does not ship), and add
a Windows #else branch with stubs that return nullptr. Consumers
link without having to repeat the OS(UNIX) guard at every call
site; at runtime the stubs short-circuit to the no-fence path.

Sandbox verification: pre-patch source reproduces the three
'no member named' errors against a synthesized MSYS2 CLANG64
configuration (OS(WINDOWS)=1, OS(UNIX)=0). Post-patch source
compiles cleanly.

---
diff --git a/Source/WebCore/platform/graphics/egl/GLFence.h b/Source/WebCore/platform/graphics/egl/GLFence.h
index 9a1a2b3..c5d4e6f 100644
--- a/Source/WebCore/platform/graphics/egl/GLFence.h	2026-07-24 08:02:55.246843800 +0000
+++ b/Source/WebCore/platform/graphics/egl/GLFence.h	2026-10-14 10:41:29.003006316 +0000
@@ -22,9 +22,11 @@
 #include <wtf/Noncopyable.h>
 #include <wtf/TZoneMalloc.h>
 
-#if OS(UNIX)
+// UnixFileDescriptor is portable to MinGW since Round 22 (Win32 SOCKET packed
+// in the descriptor payload); include it unconditionally so GLFence's
+// exportFD() / importFD() / createExportable() signatures are visible on
+// every port without each consumer having to repeat the OS(UNIX) guard.
 #include <wtf/unix/UnixFileDescriptor.h>
-#endif
 
 namespace WebCore {
 class GLDisplay;
@@ -35,17 +37,13 @@
 public:
     static bool isSupported(const GLDisplay&);
     WEBCORE_EXPORT static std::unique_ptr<GLFence> create(const GLDisplay&);
-#if OS(UNIX)
     WEBCORE_EXPORT static std::unique_ptr<GLFence> createExportable(const GLDisplay&);
     WEBCORE_EXPORT static std::unique_ptr<GLFence> importFD(const GLDisplay&, WTF::UnixFileDescriptor&&);
-#endif
     virtual ~GLFence() = default;
 
     virtual void clientWait() = 0;
     virtual void serverWait() = 0;
-#if OS(UNIX)
     virtual WTF::UnixFileDescriptor exportFD() { return { }; }
-#endif
 
 protected:
     GLFence() = default;

diff --git a/Source/WebCore/platform/graphics/egl/GLFence.cpp b/Source/WebCore/platform/graphics/egl/GLFence.cpp
index 4b5c6d7..e7f8a9b 100644
--- a/Source/WebCore/platform/graphics/egl/GLFence.cpp	2026-07-24 08:02:55.246843800 +0000
+++ b/Source/WebCore/platform/graphics/egl/GLFence.cpp	2026-10-14 10:41:40.223082213 +0000
@@ -96,6 +96,8 @@
 
     if (display.extensions().ANDROID_native_fence_sync)
         return GLFenceEGL::createExportable(display);
+#else
+    UNUSED_PARAM(display);
 #endif
     return nullptr;
 }
@@ -109,10 +111,30 @@
     if (display.extensions().ANDROID_native_fence_sync)
         return GLFenceEGL::importFD(display, WTF::move(fd));
 #else
+    UNUSED_PARAM(display);
     UNUSED_PARAM(fd);
 #endif
     return nullptr;
 }
+#else
+// MinGW: GLFence::createExportable / importFD are declared in the header
+// unconditionally (see GLFence.h), but the EGL implementation paths are
+// Unix-specific (ANDROID_native_fence_sync is a Linux DMA-Buf/EGL extension).
+// Provide Windows stubs that return nullptr so consumers (AcceleratedSurface.cpp,
+// CoordinatedPlatformLayerBufferDMABuf.cpp, OpenXRGraphicsBindingOpenGLES.cpp)
+// link without having to repeat the OS(UNIX) guard at every call site.
+std::unique_ptr<GLFence> GLFence::createExportable(const GLDisplay& display)
+{
+    UNUSED_PARAM(display);
+    return nullptr;
+}
+
+std::unique_ptr<GLFence> GLFence::importFD(const GLDisplay& display, UnixFileDescriptor&& fd)
+{
+    UNUSED_PARAM(display);
+    UNUSED_PARAM(fd);
+    return nullptr;
+}
 #endif
 
 } // namespace WebCore
From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Taozuhong <taozuhong@hotmail.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 10:46:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] MinGW: stub write() signature mismatch and fsync() absence in NotificationService.cpp

Update 35b (fixing the round-35 CLANGARM64 NotificationService.cpp
2-error block at [8293/8564], surfaced via UnifiedSource-UIProcess-36.cpp):

NotificationService.cpp:79 fails with type mismatch: MinGW-w64 <io.h>
declares write() as 'int write(int, const void*, unsigned int)' (matching
MSVCRT's _write shape: the size argument is 32-bit unsigned on Windows),
while the file-level function-pointer alias expects
'ssize_t (*)(int, const void*, size_t)' with a 64-bit size_t on x86_64.

NotificationService.cpp:104 fails with 'use of undeclared identifier fsync':
fsync() is POSIX and is not declared by MinGW-w64's <unistd.h> / <io.h>
(MSVCRT's file-flush entry point is _commit()).

Fix: replace the file-scope write-alias with a small static wrapper on
Windows that calls _write() with the size narrowed to unsigned. For
flush(), use _commit() on Windows. _commit() takes an int file descriptor
(matching m_fd.value()) and forces the CRT's internal buffer to be written
to the OS; it is the documented MSVCRT equivalent of POSIX fsync().

Sandbox verification: pre-patch source reproduces both errors against a
synthesized MSYS2 CLANGARM64 configuration. Post-patch source compiles
cleanly: _write and _commit resolve through <unistd.h> -> <io.h>.

---
diff --git a/Source/WebKit/UIProcess/Notifications/glib/NotificationService.cpp b/Source/WebKit/UIProcess/Notifications/glib/NotificationService.cpp
index 5c8e7d2..a1b2c3d 100644
--- a/Source/WebKit/UIProcess/Notifications/glib/NotificationService.cpp	2026-07-24 08:02:56.013829500 +0000
+++ b/Source/WebKit/UIProcess/Notifications/glib/NotificationService.cpp	2026-10-14 10:42:29.118412959 +0000
@@ -76,7 +76,16 @@
 static const Seconds s_dbusCallTimeout = 20_ms;
 
 // Alias to avoid conflicting with write() below.
+#if OS(WINDOWS)
+// MinGW: write() signature uses unsigned int for the size argument, not size_t;
+// wrap it to keep the (int, const void*, size_t) shape downstream consumers expect.
+static ssize_t writeToFD(int fd, const void* buffer, size_t size)
+{
+    return _write(fd, buffer, static_cast<unsigned>(size));
+}
+#else
 ssize_t (*writeToFD)(int, const void*, size_t) = write;
+#endif
 
 // Simple stream that writes to an fd.
 class FileDescriptorWriteStream : public SkWStream {
@@ -101,7 +110,13 @@
 
     void flush() final
     {
+#if OS(WINDOWS)
+        // MinGW: fsync() is POSIX; _commit() is the MSVCRT equivalent that flushes
+        // the file's buffers from the CRT internal buffer to the OS.
+        _commit(m_fd.value());
+#else
         fsync(m_fd.value());
+#endif
     };
 
     size_t bytesWritten() const final
From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Taozuhong <taozuhong@hotmail.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 11:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] MinGW: skip gio/gfiledescriptorbased.h include on Windows

Update 36 (fixing the round-36 CLANG64/CLANGARM64 NetworkCacheDataGLib.cpp
1-error block at [8502/8564], surfaced via UnifiedSource-NetworkProcess-11.cpp):

NetworkCacheDataGLib.cpp:39 fails with
  fatal error: 'gio/gfiledescriptorbased.h' file not found
   39 | #include <gio/gfiledescriptorbased.h>

The include is already guarded by `#if !PLATFORM(WIN)`, but PLATFORM(WIN)
is only true for the Windows-native WebKit port (AppleWin / WinCairo), not
for the GTK port running on Windows. On MinGW GTK (PLATFORM(GTK)=1,
PLATFORM(WIN)=0, OS(WINDOWS)=1) the guard does not trigger and the
include attempts to resolve <gio/gfiledescriptorbased.h>, which the
MSYS2 GLib build does not ship (gfiledescriptorbased.h is a Unix-only
GIO header that exposes the GFileDescriptorBased interface around
g_unix_input_stream_new_with_fd() / g_unix_output_stream_new_with_fd(),
both Linux/Unix-specific).

Inspection of the file shows that the GFileDescriptorBased interface is
never actually used in NetworkCacheDataGLib.cpp - the file only calls
g_bytes_new_with_free_func, g_bytes_new, g_bytes_get_size, g_bytes_get_data
(all from <gio/gio.h> / <glib.h>). The include is preemptive and can be
safely dropped on Windows without losing any consumed symbols.

Fix: tighten the guard from `#if !PLATFORM(WIN)` to
`#if !PLATFORM(WIN) && !OS(WINDOWS)`. This preserves the original
intent (skip on the Windows-native WebKit port) while also skipping on
the GTK-on-Windows MinGW port. No new code, no new stubs - just the
correct platform gate.

Sandbox verification: pre-patch source reproduces the
'gio/gfiledescriptorbased.h file not found' error against a
synthesized MSYS2 CLANG64/CLANGARM64 configuration (PLATFORM(GTK)=1,
OS(WINDOWS)=1, PLATFORM(WIN)=0). Post-patch source compiles cleanly:
the include is skipped on Windows, and no consumer of the
GFileDescriptorBased interface exists in the file to break.
`patch -Np1 --dry-run` on pristine+0001-0010 applies with 0 .rej
/ 0 fuzz.

---
diff --git a/Source/WebKit/NetworkProcess/cache/NetworkCacheDataGLib.cpp b/Source/WebKit/NetworkProcess/cache/NetworkCacheDataGLib.cpp
index 1a2b3c4..5d6e7f8 100644
--- a/Source/WebKit/NetworkProcess/cache/NetworkCacheDataGLib.cpp
+++ b/Source/WebKit/NetworkProcess/cache/NetworkCacheDataGLib.cpp
@@ -35,7 +35,7 @@
 #include <sys/types.h>
 #include <unistd.h>
 
-#if !PLATFORM(WIN)
+#if !PLATFORM(WIN) && !OS(WINDOWS)
 #include <gio/gfiledescriptorbased.h>
 #endif
 
From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Taozuhong <taozuhong@hotmail.com>
Date: Wed, 15 Oct 2026 02:30:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] MinGW: make IPC serialization manifests' platform variants
 mutually exclusive

Update 37 (fixing the round-36 CLANG64/CLANGARM64
WebKitPlatformGeneratedSerializers.cpp 10-error block at [8504|8460]/8564;
UCRT64 still stalls at [7041] Linking CXX static library libSkia.a - a
separate issue addressed by the PKGBUILD llvm-ar change of this round).

CI errors (identical on CLANG64 and CLANGARM64, WebKitPlatformGeneratedSerializers.cpp):

  :91   error: static assertion failed due to requirement
        'std::is_same_v<WTF::UnixFileDescriptor, WTF::Win32Handle>'
  :101  error: duplicate member 'm_handle' (Win32Handle vs previous UnixFileDescriptor)
  :107  error: static assertion failed: sizeof(ShouldBeSameSizeAsConnectionHandle)
        == sizeof(IPC::ConnectionHandle) evaluates '1 == 8'
  :137  error: redefinition of 'm_handle' (decoder.decode<Win32Handle> vs
        previous decoder.decode<UnixFileDescriptor>)
  :145  error: no matching constructor for 'IPC::ConnectionHandle' (2 arguments
        provided - both the USE(UNIX_DOMAIN_SOCKETS) and the OS(WINDOWS) branch
        of the braced initializer list are active)
  ... and the same five errors again for WebCore::SharedMemoryHandle at
  :6655/:6666/:6670/:6723/:6738 (3 arguments vs SharedMemoryHandle(Type&&, uint64_t)).

Root cause: the .serialization.in manifests declare the platform-specific
m_handle member as three INDEPENDENT #if blocks:

  #if USE(UNIX_DOMAIN_SOCKETS)
      UnixFileDescriptor m_handle;
  #endif
  #if OS(WINDOWS)
      Win32Handle m_handle;
  #endif
  #if OS(DARWIN)
      MachSendRight m_handle;
  #endif

generate-serializers.py parses each #if expression verbatim into
member.condition and emits every member variant as its own #if block
(static_assert, ShouldBeSameSizeAs member, IsIncreasing/offsetof entry,
encode statement, decode local, constructor initializer - 6 emission
sites per variant). On every upstream platform at most one of these
conditions is true, so the independent #ifs happen to be exclusive.
On MinGW GTK both USE(UNIX_DOMAIN_SOCKETS) (PlatformUse.h defines it
unconditionally for PLATFORM(GTK)||PLATFORM(WPE), even on Windows) and
OS(WINDOWS) are true simultaneously, and the generated
WebKitPlatformGeneratedSerializers.cpp becomes ill-formed.

The real C++ headers (ConnectionHandle.h:53-82, SharedMemory.h Type alias
and private members) already model this correctly with a #if/#elif/#elif
chain in which USE(UNIX_DOMAIN_SOCKETS) takes precedence; that is why the
headers themselves compile fine on MinGW GTK and only the GENERATED
serializers break. IPCSemaphore.serialization.in hit the same class of
problem in round 27 and was fixed with the identical
`OS(WINDOWS) && !USE(UNIX_DOMAIN_SOCKETS)` pattern.

Fix: make the manifest variants mirror the headers' #elif semantics by
excluding the unix flavor from the other two variants:

  #if OS(WINDOWS) && !USE(UNIX_DOMAIN_SOCKETS)
  #if OS(DARWIN) && !USE(UNIX_DOMAIN_SOCKETS)

This is a no-op on every upstream platform (Linux GTK/WPE: OS(WINDOWS)=0,
OS(DARWIN)=0; Cocoa: USE(UNIX_DOMAIN_SOCKETS)=0 so the DARWIN/WINDOWS
conditions keep their original value; WinCairo: USE(UNIX_DOMAIN_SOCKETS)=0)
and only changes behavior for the MinGW GTK combination, where the unix
flavor now wins - exactly matching the headers the generated code is
asserted against.

Files touched (no existing patch touches either file):

  Source/WebKit/Platform/IPC/ConnectionHandle.serialization.in
  Source/WebKit/Shared/WebCoreArgumentCoders.serialization.in (SharedMemoryHandle)

Verification (Linux sandbox, generator + compile-shape methodology of
rounds 27-36):

1. Generator-level: ran Scripts/generate-serializers.py over all 329
